<html>

<head>

<style>

.box {

width: 100px;

height: 100px;

color: white;

text-align: center;

line-height: 100px;

font-weight: bold;

}

.container {

width: 300px;

height: 300px;

background-color: rgb(214, 212, 185);

position: relative; /* needed for absolute example */

margin-bottom: 50px;

}
<style>
        div {
            background-color: rgb(36, 15, 139);
            padding: 10px;
        }
        div.first {
            opacity: 0.3;
            background-color: rgb(90, 165, 140);
        }
        
        div.second {
            opacity: 0.6;
            background-color: rgb(218, 179, 122);
        }

        div.third {
            opacity: 0.9;
            background-color: rgb(145, 189, 227);
        }
        </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>The opacity property</h1>
    <p>This how this property looks:</p>
    <div class="first" >opacity 0.3</div>
    <div class="second" >opacity 0.6</div>
    <div class="third" >opacity 0.9</div>
    <div><p>opacity 1 (default)</p></div>
</body>
</html>

</style>

</head>

<body>

<h2>CSS Position Examples</h2>

<div class="container">

<div class="box" style="background: rgb(110, 6, 6); position: static;">Static</div>

</div>

<div class="container">

<div class="box" style="background: rgb(13, 13, 77); position: relative; top: 20px; left: 20px;">Relative</div>

</div>

<div class="container">

<div class="box" style="background: rgb(2, 62, 2); position: absolute; top: 50px; left: 50px;">Absolute</div>

</div>

<div class="container" style="height:400px;">

<div class="box" style="background: rgb(120, 79, 4); position: fixed; top: 20px; right: 20px;">Fixed</div>

</div>

<div class="container" style="height:800px;">

<div class="box" style="background: rgb(90, 3, 90); position: sticky; top: 0;">Sticky</div>

<p>Scroll down this box to see sticky in action.</p>

<p style="margin-top:600px;">End of content</p>

</div>

</body>

</html>